# What `docker build` must NOT send to the daemon (Week 11).
#
# Everything in this file is excluded from the *build context* - the copy of the
# repository the CLI uploads to the Docker daemon before the first instruction
# runs. Excluding a path here makes the build faster, the image smaller and the
# layer cache stabler: a file that never enters the context can never invalidate
# a COPY, and can never leak into a published image.

# --- Version control and environments ---
.git/
.gitignore
.github/
venv/
.venv/
env/

# --- Python noise ---
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*.egg-info/
.pytest_cache/
.ruff_cache/

# --- Development-only parts of the repository ---
# The server imports none of these; see deployment/Dockerfile for what it does
# copy. Listed even though the Dockerfile COPYs selectively, because the context
# is uploaded before any COPY runs.
notebooks/
tests/
app/
docs/
README.md
pyproject.toml
requirements.txt

# --- Derived data and artifacts ---
# data/processed/ is rebuilt from data/raw/ by the training step in the image;
# models/*.joblib is trained during the build, so a stale local one must not be
# copied in on top of it.
data/processed/
models/

# --- OS noise ---
.DS_Store
